# Does Soften Stone cast at a stone golem's square reach it as a spell hit, and
# does it lower the golem's armour without slowing it? (inc-wqql)
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#   INCURSION_LOAD=tools/fixtures/chars/druid-shoulder-metal-seed7-opt0822.sav \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/soften-stone-golem.keys 1
# The fixture druid has wizard mode, Infinite Mana and Freeze Monsters on.
#
# THE READ. While the "Soften Stone" aim prompt is up, pressing W (wizard mode)
# on the aimed creature opens that creature's own Thing::Dump() (src/Term.cpp
# EffectPrompt), which prints "A ARM <v> (base ...)" and its Stati list. That
# dump is the oracle for armour and slow, before and after the cast. The aim
# prompt is a location-or-target prompt; the target cursor starts on the player
# square, so RIGHT enters the ring at the nearest candidate -- the golem --
# every time, however far east it stands.
#
# KEEPING OUT OF REACH. A stone golem is Large and has reach 2, and casting in
# its reach provokes a free attack: the old run died to "Catching you
# off-guard, ... slams you" in its cast-enter screen. FREEZE stops the golem's
# own turns but not that attack, and whether the attack lands is a roll of the
# dice, so standing in reach makes the run flaky. Walking away does not help:
# leaving the threatened area raises the "Abort, Flee or Disengage?" prompt and
# provoking on the way out is again a roll (src/Move.cpp). So the golem is
# SUMMONED out of reach instead. Wizard summoning places the monster with a
# pure location prompt, "Summon where?", whose cursor starts on the player and
# whose RIGHT steps it one square east (src/Debug.cpp Player::WizardOptions,
# case 6: EffectPrompt(e,Q_LOC,...)). Four RIGHTs put the golem four squares
# east: the summoned map reads "#..........@G.........#", open floor east of
# the player, and distance 4 is clear of reach 2.
SPACE
w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Soften Stone" ENTER
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Golems"
@choose "stone golem"
RIGHT*4
ENTER
@dump:summoned
@until "HP:" ESC

# BEFORE: start the cast, aim at the golem's square, dump the golem.
@until "Select Spell" m
@choose "Soften Stone"
@dump:cast-aim
RIGHT
@dump:cast-on-golem
w
@dump:before-golem
DOWN*30
@dump:before-stati

# CAST: ESC closes the wizard dump (still aiming); ENTER takes the creature
# under the cursor and fires the spell.
ESC
@dump:cast-back
ENTER
@dump:cast-enter
@until "HP:" ESC

# AFTER: aim again and dump the golem, to read the armour change and the stati.
@until "Select Spell" m
@choose "Soften Stone"
@dump:cast-aim2
RIGHT
w
@dump:after-golem
DOWN*30
@dump:after-stati
ESC
@until "HP:" ESC

# The message log, for the soften line and the absence of a slow line.
v
@dump:msglog
ESC
@quit
